1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,116
A list is a content item that holds other content items, such as

2
00:00:05,116 --> 00:00:06,704
a blog and its posts.

3
00:00:06,704 --> 00:00:09,585
This video shows how templates read a list:

4
00:00:09,585 --> 00:00:15,230
the ListPart template, and the three Liquid filters container, list_items, and list_count.

5
00:00:19,830 --> 00:00:22,519
A list is a content item with a ListPart.

6
00:00:22,519 --> 00:00:27,039
Each item inside the list carries a ContainedPart, which stores the id of

7
00:00:27,039 --> 00:00:31,730
its list, the content type of that list, and the position of the item in it.

8
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:37,077
The Lists module adds three Liquid filters that read this relationship:

9
00:00:37,077 --> 00:00:39,703
container, list_items, and list_count.

10
00:00:39,703 --> 00:00:44,240
They work in any Liquid template, not only in the templates of a list.

11
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:52,762
To display a list, the ListPart shape receives a ListPartViewModel.

12
00:00:52,762 --> 00:00:58,032
Its ContentItems property holds one page of published items, and its Pager property

13
00:00:58,032 --> 00:01:00,460
holds the links to the other pages.

14
00:01:01,210 --> 00:01:06,419
The Blog Theme overrides the template of this shape in Blog-ListPart.liquid.

15
00:01:06,419 --> 00:01:13,090
It loops over Model.ContentItems, builds the Summary display of each item, and renders Model.Pager.

16
00:01:13,090 --> 00:01:17,410
Because of its name, it applies to the Blog content type only.

17
00:01:21,610 --> 00:01:26,237
The container filter takes a content item and returns the list that holds it.

18
00:01:26,237 --> 00:01:30,139
In the Blog recipe, the Autoroute pattern of a blog post uses it

19
00:01:30,139 --> 00:01:33,540
to start each post's address with the name of its blog.

20
00:01:34,290 --> 00:01:37,389
If an item is not in a list, or its list is not

21
00:01:37,389 --> 00:01:40,371
published, container returns the item itself.

22
00:01:40,371 --> 00:01:42,651
The input must be a content item:

23
00:01:42,651 --> 00:01:44,990
anything else raises an exception.

24
00:01:49,190 --> 00:01:54,735
The list_items filter returns the content items of a list, and list_count counts them.

25
00:01:54,735 --> 00:01:58,774
Give either one a content item, or the content item id of the

26
00:01:58,774 --> 00:02:00,160
list as a string.

27
00:02:00,910 --> 00:02:06,013
Only published items count, so an item that exists only as a draft is left out.

28
00:02:06,013 --> 00:02:07,815
The filters do not page:

29
00:02:07,815 --> 00:02:12,798
list_count counts the whole list, and list_items returns all of it, sorted by

30
00:02:12,798 --> 00:02:15,500
the order stored in each ContainedPart.

31
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:22,491
Let's use all three in the template for blog posts.

32
00:02:22,491 --> 00:02:26,408
The assign tag saves the blog that container returns for the current post,

33
00:02:26,408 --> 00:02:29,982
and the template prints its title as a link, followed by its number

34
00:02:29,982 --> 00:02:31,990
of published posts from list_count.

35
00:02:32,740 --> 00:02:37,575
Then list_items returns the published posts of that blog, assign saves them in

36
00:02:37,575 --> 00:02:41,259
a variable, and a for loop prints a link to each one, with

37
00:02:41,259 --> 00:02:45,000
display_url for the address and display_text for the title.

38
00:02:45,750 --> 00:02:48,973
Add this block at the end of the post template:

39
00:02:48,973 --> 00:02:55,296
Content-BlogPost.liquid in a theme, or a template named Content__BlogPost under Design, Templates.

40
00:02:55,296 --> 00:02:59,735
A template saved in the admin takes priority over the theme file of

41
00:02:59,735 --> 00:03:02,410
the same name, so it must be complete.

42
00:03:04,023 --> 00:03:10,275
In the admin, Design, Templates lists the template under its name, Content__BlogPost.

43
00:03:10,275 --> 00:03:13,573
It applies to the page of every blog post.

44
00:03:14,029 --> 00:03:17,790
On the page of a blog post, the block follows the content.

45
00:03:17,790 --> 00:03:22,903
The heading links back to the blog, and list_count reports three published posts,

46
00:03:22,903 --> 00:03:25,429
although the blog also holds a draft.

47
00:03:25,879 --> 00:03:30,045
Below the count, the loop prints a link to each published post.

48
00:03:30,045 --> 00:03:35,479
The draft is missing from the list, because list_items returns published items only.

49
00:03:39,679 --> 00:03:44,278
In a Razor view, the Orchard helper offers the same two queries:

50
00:03:44,278 --> 00:03:47,890
QueryListItemsAsync and QueryListItemsCountAsync.

51
00:03:47,890 --> 00:03:50,189
Both take the id of the list.

52
00:03:50,939 --> 00:03:55,153
An optional second argument is a predicate on the content item index.

53
00:03:55,153 --> 00:03:57,906
It replaces the default of published items:

54
00:03:57,906 --> 00:04:01,839
a predicate on the Latest property of the index includes drafts.

55
00:04:03,839 --> 00:04:06,040
That is how templates read a list:

56
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:10,387
the ListPart shape renders one page of items, container finds the list of

57
00:04:10,387 --> 00:04:15,009
an item, and list_items and list_count work on every published item of a list.

58
00:04:15,009 --> 00:04:16,439
Thanks for watching.

